  ("h2", "The About section: only the first two lines are read"),
  ("p", "LinkedIn truncates About behind a \"see more\" link. Whatever is above that fold is the entire section for most readers, so <strong>the first sentence must be the summary of you</strong>, written in plain declarative form."),
  ("p", "The structure that works below the fold: what you do now, one or two specific pieces of proof with numbers, your stack, and what you want next, ending with contact details. Short paragraphs. No walls of text — the mobile app renders them as a grey slab nobody finishes."),
  ("h2", "Experience entries are not job descriptions"),
  ("p", "Copying your duties from the job posting is the most common waste of space on LinkedIn. Write what changed because you were there. Action, object, method, result — with the result quantified when it honestly can be."),
  ("formula", "Instead of: Responsible for maintaining internal reporting tools\nWrite:      Rebuilt the internal reporting pipeline over 50+ daily sources,\n            cutting manual research time 60%"),
