  ("What should a LinkedIn headline contain?", "What you are, one proof point or specialisation, your concrete stack in the industry's own terms, and what you are building or seeking. Use most of the roughly 220 characters, and avoid words like passionate, aspiring, ninja, or guru, which are neither searched nor informative."),
  ("How long should the About section be?", "Structurally, only the first two lines matter, because LinkedIn truncates the rest behind a see-more link. Lead with a plain declarative summary of who you are, then use short paragraphs for proof with numbers, your stack, what you want next, and contact details."),
